# Implementation Plan - Precision Pipeline Cleanup & Deployment

The user's restoration pipeline is stuck at 0%, despite successful uploads. Additionally, redundant status labels ("RECEIVED", "DECOMPRESSING") persist on the dashboard, and a port conflict is preventing the latest Nginx configuration from deploying.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hydration Mismatch:** The "Minified React errors" seen in the logs are caused by using `new Date().toLocaleTimeString()` in the component's render method. I will move this to a `useEffect` to ensure the server and client renders match.

> [!WARNING]
> **Port 80 Conflict:** Port 80 is currently occupied by a host-level process. If I cannot stop it, I will prepare a fallback to port 81 or another available port to ensure the new UI is accessible.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Dashboard UI Simplification
I will stripping all redundant text from the "Readiness" card to keep it clean and focused purely on the extraction percentage.

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/app/page.tsx)
- Remove "Profiling Stream", "Initializing", and specific MB counts from the `getReadiness` return values.
- Return only the percentage (e.g., `80%`) or a single high-level status word when appropriate.

#### [MODIFY] [UploadCard.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/components/UploadCard.tsx)
- Move all dynamic time string generation into a `useEffect` to fix hydration errors.
- Ensure the "Decompressing & Extracting" labels match the user's preferred industrial style without being redundant to the Readiness card.

### 2. Pipeline Robustness (The 0% Stall)
I will add diagnostic checks to the restoration loop to find out why data isn't flowing into the staging schema.

#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- Add `logger.info` at the exact moment the `psql` pipe is opened.
- Implement a binary path check (using `shutil.which`) to verify `gunzip` and `psql` exist before starting.
- Add logging for the first 5MB chunk to confirm the "Sync" is actually occurring.

### 3. Infrastructure & Deployment
#### [MODIFY] [docker-compose.yml](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/docker/docker-compose.yml)
- Change host port mapping for Nginx to `8081:80` (fallback) or resolve the `address already in use` error if possible.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- `docker logs -f sqauto_api`: Monitor for new "Industrial Restoration Started" logs.
- `docker compose ps`: Verify all containers, including Nginx, are `Up`.

### Manual Verification
1. Upload the 114MB dump again.
2. Confirm the Readiness card shows ONLY the percentage.
3. Open the "Live Pipeline Insight" and verify the log stream is active.
4. Verify the React hydration errors in the browser console are gone.
